    rdfs:comment "Actuators are physical devices that convert an electrical, hydraulic, or pneumatic control signal into mechanical motion or force, enabling a control system to produce a desired physical effect in the world. They are the output components of robotic and cyber-physical systems, spanning technologies including servo motors, pneumatic cylinders, hydraulic actuators, and piezoelectric elements, each offering different trade-offs in force output, speed, precision, and energy efficiency."@en ;
