    rdfs:comment "An Airdrop is a token distribution mechanism in which a blockchain project allocates free tokens to a set of wallet addresses, typically to bootstrap a community, reward early users or decentralise ownership. Eligibility may be based on prior on-chain activity, holdings of another asset or completion of tasks. Airdrops are a marketing and governance tool but attract Sybil attacks that the project must mitigate."@en ;
