ngm:api-contract a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An API contract is the agreed, machine-readable specification of how a service may be called and what it will return, covering endpoints, request and response schemas, data types, status codes and error semantics. It functions as a formal agreement between the provider and consumers of an interface, allowing each side to develop and test independently against a shared definition. Expressed in formats such as OpenAPI or GraphQL schemas, the contract enables tooling for validation, mocking, code generation and compatibility checking across versions."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Api Contract"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:data-schema ;
