ngm:api-design a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "API design is the discipline of specifying the contract, structure, and behaviour of an application programming interface so that it is consistent, intuitive, evolvable, and reliable for the developers who consume it. It covers resource and operation modelling, naming and conventions, request and response schemas, error semantics, authentication, versioning, and documentation, balancing usability against the constraints of the underlying system. Good API design treats the interface as a long-lived product whose contract must remain stable and backward-compatible while still allowing the implementation behind it to evolve."@en ;
    rdfs:label "API Design"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:software-architecture ;
