ngm:ar-interoperability a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "AR interoperability is the capacity for augmented reality content, spatial anchors, and experiences to function consistently across different hardware devices, operating systems, and rendering engines. It depends on shared data formats for spatial maps and anchors, common coordinate reference conventions, and standardised APIs for camera, tracking, and rendering access, as pursued by efforts such as the ETSI Augmented Reality Framework. Without it, AR content authored for one platform typically requires substantial rework to run on another, fragmenting the content ecosystem and raising development cost. It is a prerequisite for shared, persistent AR experiences that multiple users on different devices can view and manipulate together."@en ;
    rdfs:label "AR Interoperability"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:cross-platform-interoperability ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "ar-interoperability" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "spatial-computing" .
ngm:ar-occlusion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "AR occlusion is the computational technique by which virtual objects rendered in an augmented reality scene are correctly hidden or partially hidden by real-world geometry that physically lies in front of them from the viewer's perspective. Achieving occlusion requires real-time estimation of the depth structure of the physical scene, typically via depth sensors or monocular depth estimation neural networks, so that the rendering pipeline can apply correct depth ordering between real and virtual content. Without occlusion, virtual objects appear to float unconvincingly in front of all physical surfaces regardless of their spatial relationship."@en ;
    rdfs:label "AR Occlusion"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:augmented-reality ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:sc-display-and-rendering ;
    skos:broader ngm:sc-display-and-rendering ;
    vc:enables ngm:real-time-rendering ;
    vc:enables ngm:spatial-mapping ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.8"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:mixed-reality ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:occlusion-rendering ;
    vc:slug "ar-occlusion" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "spatial-computing" ;
    vc:uses ngm:computer-vision ;
    vc:uses ngm:depth-estimation ;
    vc:uses ngm:scene-understanding .
ngm:ar-overlay a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "AR Overlay refers to the digital layer of virtual elements including holograms, data visualizations, animations, and 3D objects that are spatially anchored and rendered over the user's view of the physical world in augmented reality systems, creating a seamless blend of virtual and real content."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Ar Overlay"@en ;
