ngm:asset-transfer a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Asset transfer is the act of moving ownership or control of a digital asset from one party or address to another, recorded as a state change on a ledger. It is the basic operation that custody arrangements must secure and that digital-ownership systems rely on to change the recorded holder of a token or asset. Cross-chain and tokenised real-world-asset transfer are specialised forms that move value across ledgers or between on-chain and off-chain representations."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Asset Transfer"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:custody ;
