ngm:backdrivability a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Backdrivability is the property of a mechanical actuator or transmission that allows external forces applied at the output to drive the input in reverse, so motion and force pass freely in both directions. A highly backdrivable joint exhibits low reflected inertia and friction, enabling it to comply with and sense external contact. It is a key enabler of safe, compliant physical human-robot interaction and force-controlled robots."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Backdrivability"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:actuator ;
