ngm:behavior-analysis a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Behavior Analysis is an AI and machine learning technique concerned with the systematic observation, modelling, and interpretation of patterns in entity actions — whether human users, software agents, or autonomous systems — in order to detect anomalies, predict future actions, or classify intent. It combines statistical modelling, sequence analysis, and supervised or unsupervised learning to extract actionable intelligence from behavioural streams. Typical applications include cybersecurity threat detection, user experience optimisation, game AI design, and fraud prevention."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Behavior Analysis"@en ;
