ngm:belief-propagation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Belief propagation is a message-passing algorithm for performing inference on graphical models by iteratively exchanging local messages between nodes representing variables and the factors that relate them. On tree-structured graphs it computes exact marginal distributions; on graphs with cycles, loopy belief propagation provides an approximate inference scheme that often works well in practice. It is the basis of efficient decoding for modern error-correcting codes and of probabilistic reasoning over structured domains."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Belief Propagation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:graphical-model ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:probabilistic-inference ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r2932 ;
