ngm:blackboard-pattern a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A coordination architecture in which multiple specialised agents collaborate not by messaging each other directly but by reading from and writing to a shared, structured workspace — the blackboard. Each agent watches the blackboard for a state it can act on, contributes its partial result back to the shared space, and lets other agents build on that contribution in turn, so a solution accretes incrementally through many opportunistic updates rather than through a fixed pipeline. The pattern decouples the collaborators from one another: an agent needs to understand only the blackboard's contents, not the identity, order, or availability of its peers."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Blackboard Pattern"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:multi-agent-orchestration ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:multiagentorchestration ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r3272 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r3273 ;
