ngm:bytecode a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Bytecode is a compact, platform-independent instruction set produced by compiling source code, designed to be executed by a virtual machine rather than directly by hardware. In blockchain systems, smart contracts written in high-level languages such as Solidity are compiled to bytecode that the Ethereum Virtual Machine deterministically executes across every node. Bytecode strikes a balance between the portability of source code and the efficiency of native machine code."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Bytecode"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:smart-contract-execution ;
