ngm:carbon-credit-retirement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Carbon credit retirement is the permanent cancellation of a carbon credit in a registry so that it can no longer be sold, transferred, or double-counted, formally claiming the underlying emission reduction or removal. Retirement is the terminal step that converts a tradable credit into a fulfilled offset claim against a specific buyer's emissions. It is fundamental to carbon market integrity because it guarantees that each tonne of avoided or removed CO2 is claimed only once."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Carbon Credit Retirement"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:economic-mechanism ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
