ngm:cellular-automata a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A cellular automaton is a discrete computational model consisting of a regular grid of cells, each holding one of a finite set of states, that evolve over discrete time steps according to a fixed local update rule applied uniformly across the grid. The next state of a cell depends only on its current state and the states of a defined neighbourhood, yet iterated application of simple local rules can produce complex, emergent global behaviour. Cellular automata are used to study self-organisation and computational universality, and serve as lightweight simulation substrates for physical, biological and social systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Cellular Automata"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:computational-model ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:isPartOf ngm:computational-model ;
