ngm:cloud-native-architecture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Cloud-native architecture is an approach to designing and operating applications that fully exploit elastic, on-demand cloud infrastructure. It favours loosely coupled, independently deployable services packaged in containers, orchestrated dynamically, and managed through automation, declarative configuration and continuous delivery. The goal is resilient, scalable systems that can be evolved rapidly and recover automatically from failure."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Cloud-Native Architecture"@en ;
