ngm:collaboration-platform a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Collaboration Platform is an integrated software environment that unifies communication channels, shared workspaces, workflow automation, and content management tooling to enable coordinated work among distributed teams. Such platforms expose API-first architectures built atop real-time messaging protocols, WebRTC-based media pipelines, and cloud storage with conflict resolution, providing a composable substrate for synchronous and asynchronous teamwork. Enterprise-grade deployments layer in identity federation, data residency controls, compliance archiving, and extensible integration ecosystems, while modern platforms increasingly embed AI-driven capabilities such as meeting transcription, action-item extraction, and intelligent search. The category spans lightweight messaging tools through full unified-communications suites and extends into spatial and immersive collaboration modalities."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Collaboration Platform"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:distributed-systems ;
