ngm:conversion-rate-optimisation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Conversion rate optimisation (CRO) is the systematic practice of increasing the percentage of visitors to a digital property who complete a desired action — purchasing, subscribing, registering — by forming hypotheses about user behaviour and testing changes to copy, design, pricing, and flow. It combines quantitative instrumentation such as funnel analytics and A/B and multivariate testing with qualitative research such as session recordings and user interviews, turning traffic acquired through marketing into measurable business outcomes."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Conversion Rate Optimisation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:digital-marketing ;
