ngm:crowdfunding a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Crowdfunding is a financing model in which a project or venture raises capital from a large number of contributors, each providing a relatively small amount, typically through an online platform. Models range from donation and reward-based campaigns to equity and debt offerings, and blockchain variants use token sales to distribute ownership or utility rights. The approach broadens access to early-stage capital while distributing risk across many backers."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Crowdfunding"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:de-fi ;
