ngm:data-models a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Data models are the collected structural specifications that define how information is represented, related and constrained within a system or framework. In digital-twin and layered service architectures they describe the shape of state, telemetry and interactions exchanged between components. Well-defined data models are a prerequisite for interoperability, validation and consistent behaviour across service layers."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Data Models"@en ;
