ngm:data-residency a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The physical or geographic location in which an organisation's data is stored and processed, and the practice of controlling that location to satisfy regulatory, contractual, tax, or policy requirements; data residency underpins localisation mandates and sovereignty claims by determining which jurisdiction's laws, courts, and government access powers apply to the data."@en ;
