ngm:demographic-parity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Demographic parity is a group-fairness criterion requiring that a model's positive prediction rate be equal across protected groups, independent of the true label. Also called statistical parity, it is satisfied when the probability of a favourable decision does not depend on membership of a protected attribute such as gender or ethnicity. It is one of several formal, often mutually incompatible, definitions of algorithmic fairness."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Demographic Parity"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:algorithmic-fairness ;
