    rdfs:comment "The process of reconstructing in-memory data structures or objects from a serialised byte stream or textual encoding such as JSON, XML, or Protocol Buffers, reversing serialisation so that transmitted or persisted state can be used by a running program. Deserialisation must validate structure, types, and bounds of untrusted input, since naive object reconstruction is a well-known source of remote-code-execution vulnerabilities."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Deserialisation"@en ;
