ngm:detailed-balance a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Detailed balance is a condition on a Markov chain stating that, in equilibrium, the probability flux between any two states is equal in both directions. When a transition kernel satisfies detailed balance with respect to a target distribution, that distribution is a stationary distribution of the chain. It is the central design principle behind most Markov chain Monte Carlo samplers, including Metropolis-Hastings."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Detailed Balance"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:equilibrium-condition ;
