ngm:differentiability a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Differentiability is the mathematical property of a function having a well-defined derivative at every point in its domain, allowing gradients to be computed via calculus. In machine learning it is a prerequisite for gradient-based optimisation: activation and cost functions must be differentiable, or approximately so, for backpropagation to compute parameter updates. Non-differentiable operations require relaxations, subgradients, or surrogate approximations to remain trainable."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiability"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:calculus ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.55"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "differentiability" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "machine-learning" .
ngm:differentiable-architecture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Differentiable Architecture refers to a neural network design paradigm, most prominently realised in Differentiable Architecture Search (DARTS), in which discrete structural choices — such as which operation to place at each edge of a candidate graph or how to connect layers — are relaxed to continuous mixture weights over a predefined set of operations. This relaxation renders the architecture selection problem differentiable, allowing the architecture parameters to be optimised jointly with network weights via gradient descent on a validation loss. Once optimised, the continuous mixture is discretised to yield a final architecture, dramatically reducing the computational cost of neural architecture search compared to evolutionary or reinforcement learning methods."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Architecture"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-model-architecture ;
    skos:broader ngm:ai-model-architecture ;
    vc:enables ngm:machine-learning-discipline ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:deep-learning ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:hyperparameter ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:knowledge-distillation ;
    vc:slug "differentiable-architecture" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "artificial-intelligence" ;
    vc:uses ngm:gradient-descent ;
    vc:uses ngm:neural-network-architecture .
ngm:differentiable-function a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A differentiable function is one that has a well-defined derivative at every point in its domain, meaning it can be locally approximated by a linear map. Neural network components must be differentiable, or approximated by a differentiable surrogate, for gradient-based optimisation to compute usable error signals. Automatic differentiation and backpropagation both depend on the composed network being a differentiable function of its parameters."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Function"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:calculus ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-draft ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "differentiable-function" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "machine-learning" .
ngm:differentiable-lookup a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Lookup"@en .
ngm:differentiable-physics a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Physics"@en .
ngm:differentiable-programming a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Differentiable programming is a programming paradigm in which entire programs, not just isolated functions, are constructed so that gradients can be computed automatically through them via automatic differentiation. It treats control flow, loops and composed functions as differentiable building blocks, enabling gradient-based optimisation of arbitrary computational pipelines rather than only fixed neural network layers. It underlies techniques such as normalising flows, where a chain of invertible, differentiable transformations must be optimised end-to-end."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Programming"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:programming-paradigm ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r7840 ;
    vc:enables ngm:normalising-flows ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:isPartOf ngm:programming-paradigm ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.55"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:requires ngm:automatic-differentiation ;
    vc:slug "differentiable-programming" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "machine-learning" .
ngm:differentiable-rasteriser a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Rasteriser"@en .
ngm:differentiable-rasterizer a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Rasterizer"@en .
ngm:differentiable-rendering a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Differentiable rendering is a class of algorithms that reformulate the image-formation pipeline so that pixel values are differentiable with respect to scene parameters — including geometry, surface materials, lighting, and camera pose. By enabling backpropagation through the rendering process, these methods support gradient-based optimisation for inverse rendering, scene reconstruction from 2D observations, and end-to-end training of 3D-aware neural models. The field bridges classical computer graphics with deep learning, treating rendering as a learnable, differentiable module within a larger neural architecture."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Differentiable Rendering"@en ;
