ngm:digital-signal-processor a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A digital signal processor (DSP) is a specialised microprocessor architecture optimised for the high-throughput numerical operations of digital signal processing, such as multiply-accumulate, filtering and fast transforms. DSPs feature hardware support for fixed and floating-point arithmetic, parallel datapaths and efficient memory access to process audio, sensor and communication signals in real time at low power. They are a core building block of audio systems, embedded devices and spatial computing hardware."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Digital Signal Processor"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:audio-system ;
