ngm:disaster-response a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Disaster response is the coordinated use of sensing, mapping and robotic systems to assess damage, locate survivors and direct relief in the aftermath of natural or human-made catastrophes. Spatial-computing techniques fuse aerial imagery, LiDAR, satellite remote sensing and ground-robot telemetry into situational maps that guide responders. Speed, robustness under degraded conditions, and accurate geospatial localisation are the defining requirements."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Disaster Response"@en ;
