    vc:slug "domain-access-control" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "metaverse" .
ngm:domain-adaptation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Domain adaptation is a sub-field of transfer learning that addresses the domain shift problem: a model trained on a labelled source distribution degrades when applied to a target distribution whose marginal or conditional statistics differ. Methods fall into feature-alignment approaches (learning domain-invariant representations via adversarial training, maximum mean discrepancy minimisation, or optimal transport), instance re-weighting schemes that correct for covariate shift, and self-training or pseudo-labelling strategies that exploit unlabelled target data. It spans unsupervised, semi-supervised, and multi-source settings and underpins practical deployment of models in NLP, computer vision, speech recognition, and scientific computing wherever labelled target data is scarce or costly."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Domain Adaptation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-technique ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:machine-learning-discipline ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:representation-learning ;
