ngm:encoder-decoder a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The encoder-decoder is a neural network architecture pattern in which an encoder maps a variable-length input into an intermediate representation and a decoder generates a variable-length output conditioned on that representation. It underpins sequence-to-sequence learning for machine translation, speech recognition, and speech synthesis, and appears in both recurrent and transformer instantiations, usually augmented with an attention mechanism so the decoder can consult the full encoded input at every generation step rather than a single fixed-size vector."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Encoder-Decoder"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:neural-network ;
    vc:enables ngm:machine-translation ;
    vc:enables ngm:speech-recognition ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-draft ;
    vc:isPartOf ngm:acoustic-model ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.8"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:recurrent-neural-network ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:transformer ;
    vc:slug "encoder-decoder" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "machine-learning" ;
    vc:uses ngm:attention-mechanism .
ngm:encoder-decoder-architecture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A neural network design pattern comprising an encoder that compresses an input sequence into a latent representation and a decoder that generates an output sequence from that representation, enabling sequence-to-sequence mappings for tasks such as machine translation, summarisation, and image captioning. The architecture underpins the original Transformer (Vaswani et al., 2017) and models such as T5 and BART."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Encoder Decoder Architecture"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-model-architecture ;
