ngm:epidemiological-modelling a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Epidemiological modelling is the use of mathematical and computational models to describe how infectious diseases spread through populations over time. Compartmental models partition a population into states such as susceptible, infected, and recovered, and use differential equations to govern transitions between them, while network and agent-based models capture heterogeneous contact structures. These models inform forecasting, intervention design, and public-health policy."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Epidemiological Modelling"@en ;
