ngm:fairness-in-machine-learning a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Fairness in machine learning is the study and practice of ensuring that learned models do not produce systematically disadvantageous outcomes for individuals or groups defined by protected attributes such as race, gender, or age. It encompasses formal fairness criteria — including demographic parity, equalised odds, and individual fairness — and the techniques used to measure and mitigate disparate impact before, during, or after training. The field is central to responsible and ethical AI, balancing accuracy with equitable treatment."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Fairness in Machine Learning"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:responsible-ai ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r10328 ;
