ngm:false-positive a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A false positive is an outcome in which a classifier or detection system reports the positive class for an instance that actually belongs to the negative class. It is one of the four cells of a confusion matrix and corresponds to a Type I error in statistical terms. The rate of false positives directly shapes precision and specificity and is traded off against false negatives when a decision threshold is tuned."@en ;
    rdfs:label "False Positive"@en ;
