ngm:filtration a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "In probability theory, a filtration is an increasing family of sigma-algebras indexed by time that formally represents the accumulation of information available up to each instant. It models what is knowable at each point as a stochastic process unfolds, with each sigma-algebra containing all events whose outcomes are determined by then. Filtrations are fundamental to defining adapted processes, martingales, and conditional expectations in stochastic analysis and mathematical finance."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Filtration"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:machine-learning-discipline-technique ;
