    rdfs:comment "A flat panel display is a thin, lightweight electronic display that produces images on a flat surface using technologies such as liquid crystal, organic light-emitting diode or micro-LED panels. It contrasts with bulky cathode-ray-tube displays and forms the dominant display category for monitors, mobile devices and near-eye optics in head-mounted hardware. Key characteristics include resolution, refresh rate, contrast and pixel density."@en ;
