ngm:frequentist-statistics a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The school of statistical inference that defines probability as long-run relative frequency over repeated sampling, treats parameters as fixed unknowns rather than random variables, and evaluates procedures — estimators, hypothesis tests, confidence intervals — by their repeated-sampling operating characteristics such as bias, error rates, and coverage, in explicit contrast to Bayesian inference over posterior beliefs."@en ;
