    rdfs:comment "Full-duplex communication is a mode of data exchange in which both endpoints can transmit and receive simultaneously over a single connection. It contrasts with half-duplex, where only one side may send at a time. Full-duplex channels enable low-latency, bidirectional interaction and are central to technologies such as web sockets and real-time messaging."@en ;
