ngm:gaussian-process-regression a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Gaussian process regression is a non-parametric Bayesian method that models an unknown function as a distribution over functions defined by a mean and a covariance (kernel) function. Given observations, it produces a posterior that yields predictions together with calibrated uncertainty estimates. It is widely used where data is scarce and quantified uncertainty matters, such as Bayesian optimisation and surrogate modelling."@en ;
