ngm:geospatial-data a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Geospatial data is information explicitly tied to a location on or near the Earth's surface, expressed through coordinates, geometries, or raster grids. It encompasses vector features (points, lines, polygons), satellite and aerial imagery, elevation models, point clouds, and attributes associated with places. Such data underpins mapping, navigation, remote sensing, logistics, urban planning, and spatial analysis across many domains."@en ;
