ngm:h-bridge a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An H-bridge is a power-electronics circuit of four switching elements arranged in an 'H' around a load, enabling voltage of either polarity to be applied from a single supply. It is the core stage of DC motor drivers: diagonal switch pairs drive the motor forward or reverse, pulse-width modulation of the switches regulates speed and torque, and shorting or opening both legs provides braking or coasting. Implemented with MOSFETs or IGBTs plus gate drivers and protection, H-bridges power robotics actuators, servo drives, inverters, and battery-powered traction."@en ;
    rdfs:label "H-Bridge"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:power-electronics ;
    vc:enables ngm:motor-control ;
