ngm:hand-tracking-telepresence a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Hand Tracking Telepresence is the real-time capture, transmission, and rendering of hand pose and gesture data from a remote participant into a local or shared virtual environment. It enables natural gestural communication — such as pointing, waving, or manipulating shared objects — between geographically distributed collaborators. By preserving expressive hand movements, this technology significantly enriches the non-verbal communication channel in remote collaboration systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Hand Tracking Telepresence"@en ;
