ngm:hateoas a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "HATEOAS, hypermedia as the engine of application state, is the REST constraint requiring that a client interact with an application entirely through hypermedia links and controls supplied dynamically by the server in its responses. Rather than hard-coding endpoint structures, the client discovers available actions and transitions at runtime by following links the server provides, mirroring how a browser navigates the web. This constraint decouples clients from fixed URI schemes and is the distinguishing feature of a fully RESTful, self-describing API."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Hateoas"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:rest ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r11576 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r11577 ;
