    rdfs:comment "The Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is an application-layer, request-response protocol for exchanging hypermedia documents and data across the web. Clients issue requests with methods and headers, and servers return responses with status codes and content. HTTP is the foundational protocol of the World Wide Web and of most modern web APIs."@en ;
