    rdfs:comment "Image Classification is the computer vision task of assigning a categorical label to an entire image from a predefined set of classes, determining what is depicted in the image as a whole. Modern image classification employs deep convolutional neural networks (ResNet, EfficientNet, Vision Transformers) trained on large-scale datasets such as ImageNet to achieve human-level or super-human performance on diverse visual recognition tasks."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Image Classification"@en ;
