ngm:image-recognition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Image recognition is the computer-vision task of identifying and categorising the objects, scenes, people or attributes present in a digital image. It maps raw pixel data to semantic labels, ranging from whole-image classification through to localisation of multiple distinct entities within a single frame. Modern image recognition is dominated by deep convolutional and transformer-based neural networks trained on large labelled datasets, which learn hierarchical visual features rather than relying on hand-engineered descriptors."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Image Recognition"@en ;
