ngm:inductive-bias a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Inductive bias is the set of assumptions a learning algorithm uses to generalise from finite training data to unseen inputs. Because infinitely many functions fit any finite sample, a learner must prefer some hypotheses over others, and that preference — encoded in model architecture, regularisation, priors, or the choice of hypothesis space — is its inductive bias. Appropriate inductive bias is what lets a model extrapolate sensibly rather than merely memorise."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Inductive Bias"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-research-area ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:machine-learning-discipline ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r12430 ;
