ngm:initial-coin-offering a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An initial coin offering (ICO) is a blockchain-based fundraising mechanism in which a project issues and sells newly created cryptographic tokens to early backers, typically in exchange for established cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin or Ether. Tokens are usually distributed via smart contracts and may grant utility within a planned protocol, governance rights, or speculative value. Pioneered around 2013–2017, ICOs enabled permissionless global capital formation but attracted intense regulatory scrutiny over investor protection and securities classification, prompting more structured successors such as security token offerings and initial exchange offerings."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Coin Offering"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:cryptocurrency-token ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r12602 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r12603 ;
    vc:bridgesTo ngm:initial-dex-offering ;
    vc:bridgesTo ngm:initial-exchange-offering ;
    vc:contrastsWith ngm:initial-public-offering ;
    vc:contrastsWith ngm:security-token-offering ;
    vc:dependsOn ngm:ethereum ;
    vc:enables ngm:capital-formation ;
    vc:enables ngm:decentralised-fundraising ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:hasPart ngm:token-sale ;
    vc:hasPart ngm:whitepaper ;
    vc:isPartOf ngm:token-economics ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.62"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:crowdfunding ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:securities-regulation ;
    vc:requires ngm:cryptocurrency-wallet ;
    vc:slug "initial-coin-offering" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "blockchain" ;
    vc:supports ngm:protocol-bootstrapping ;
    vc:supports ngm:utility-token ;
    vc:uses ngm:erc-20-token-standard ;
    vc:uses ngm:smart-contract .
ngm:initial-dex-offering a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An initial DEX offering (IDO) is a token fundraising and distribution model in which a new token is launched directly on a decentralised exchange, with liquidity provided into an automated market maker pool so trading begins immediately. Unlike centralised or regulated offerings, an IDO is permissionless and settled on-chain through smart contracts, often using launchpads that manage allocation and anti-bot measures. It contrasts with the initial coin offering and the regulated initial public offering by emphasising immediate liquidity and decentralised access."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Initial Dex Offering"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:token-sale ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r12604 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r12605 ;
    vc:bridgesTo ngm:security-token-offering ;
    vc:contrastsWith ngm:initial-coin-offering ;
