ngm:integrated-circuit a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An integrated circuit (IC) is a set of electronic circuits — transistors, resistors, capacitors and their interconnections — fabricated as a single monolithic device on a wafer of semiconductor material, usually silicon. By miniaturising and mass-producing complete circuits photolithographically, ICs made computation cheap, fast and reliable, enabling microprocessors, memory, FPGAs and application-specific chips; transistor density doubled roughly every two years in the trend described by Moore's Law, underpinning the whole of modern digital infrastructure."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Integrated Circuit"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:hardware ;
