ngm:key-ceremony a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A key ceremony is a carefully scripted, audited procedure for generating, distributing, or activating cryptographic keys under strict controls and witnessed participation. It is used when the keys involved are so sensitive that their creation must be verifiably correct, tamper-evident, and resistant to insider compromise. Key ceremonies are common in certificate authorities, threshold-cryptography setups, and high-value custody systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Key Ceremony"@en ;
