ngm:keyframe-animation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Keyframe animation is a technique in which an animator specifies an object's properties at a set of significant frames, called keyframes, and the system interpolates the in-between frames automatically. Property values such as position, rotation, and scale are stored on timed curves whose interpolation and easing control the motion between keys. It is a foundational method for authoring deterministic, repeatable motion in computer graphics and real-time engines."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Keyframe Animation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:animation ;
