ngm:kqml a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "KQML, the Knowledge Query and Manipulation Language, is an early agent communication language and protocol for exchanging information and knowledge among software agents. It defines a set of performatives, message types grounded in speech-act theory, that express the intent of a communication such as ask, tell, subscribe or achieve. KQML influenced later standards including the FIPA Agent Communication Language."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Kqml"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:agent-communication-language ;
