ngm:low-rank-adaptation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) is a parameter-efficient fine-tuning method that injects trainable low-rank decomposition matrices into the weight matrices of a frozen pre-trained model, enabling task adaptation with a fraction of the trainable parameters required by full fine-tuning."@en ;
