ngm:market-access a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Market access is the ability of a product, service or system to be lawfully sold and adopted within a target jurisdiction or sector, conditioned on meeting regulatory, certification and conformity requirements. For robotic and physical-automation systems it depends on demonstrating compliance with safety, electromagnetic and product-directive obligations such as CE marking before placement on a market. Achieving market access is therefore a gateway to commercialisation rather than a purely commercial activity."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Market Access"@en ;
