ngm:market-efficiency a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Market efficiency is the degree to which asset prices fully and rapidly reflect all available information, leaving no systematic opportunity for risk-adjusted excess returns. The efficient-market hypothesis frames it in weak, semi-strong, and strong forms according to the information set incorporated. Higher efficiency implies accurate price signals, lower transaction costs, and effective capital allocation."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Market Efficiency"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:economic-mechanism ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
