ngm:message-passing-interface a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Message Passing Interface (MPI) is a standardised communication protocol and application programming interface for parallel and distributed computing. It defines primitives for point-to-point and collective communication between processes running across multiple compute nodes, enabling tightly coupled high-performance computing workloads. MPI is the de facto standard for scientific computing, numerical simulations, and distributed AI training at supercomputer scale."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Message Passing Interface"@en ;
