ngm:mixed-precision-training a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A training technique that uses lower precision (FP16 or BF16) for most computations whilst maintaining higher precision (FP32) for numerically critical operations, reducing memory usage and increasing training speed without sacrificing model quality. Relies on loss scaling to prevent gradient underflow and leverages hardware tensor cores for throughput gains."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed Precision Training"@en ;
