ngm:multi-objective-optimisation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Multi-objective optimisation is the discipline of optimising two or more conflicting objective functions simultaneously, where improving one objective typically degrades another. Rather than a single optimum it yields a Pareto front of non-dominated trade-off solutions, from which a decision-maker selects according to preferences. It is solved with scalarisation, evolutionary, and gradient-based methods and is pervasive in engineering design, machine learning, and resource allocation."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Multi Objective Optimisation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:optimisation ;
