ngm:network-effects a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Network effects describe the phenomenon whereby a product or service gains additional value for each existing user as the number of participants increases, creating a self-reinforcing growth dynamic. Direct network effects arise when users directly benefit from others on the same platform; indirect effects emerge when complementary products or services multiply with scale, creating cross-side externalities."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Network Effects"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:positive-feedback ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r15249 ;
