ngm:noise-cancellation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Noise cancellation is the process of reducing or eliminating unwanted audio signals from a primary audio stream using signal processing techniques. Active noise cancellation generates an anti-phase signal to destructively interfere with the noise, while passive methods use physical barriers. The technique is applied in audio hardware, telecommunications, and AI-driven speech enhancement systems to improve clarity and intelligibility."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Noise Cancellation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-technique ;
