ngm:non-convex-optimisation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The minimisation of objective functions that are not convex, so the loss surface may contain multiple local minima, saddle points, plateaus, and ravines, and no general guarantee links a local solution to the global optimum. Non-convex optimisation is the actual setting of deep learning—neural network training landscapes are highly non-convex—and of many engineering problems, tackled in practice with stochastic gradient methods, momentum, restarts, relaxations, and problem-specific structure rather than the clean certificates available in the convex case."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Non-Convex Optimisation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:mathematical-optimisation ;
