ngm:nonverbal-communication a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Nonverbal communication is the transmission of meaning through cues other than words, including facial expression, gaze, gesture, posture, interpersonal distance, and tone of voice. It conveys emotion, regulates interaction, and signals social presence, and it is central to creating believable avatars and co-presence in virtual and augmented reality. Reproducing nonverbal channels faithfully is a core challenge for embodied and immersive collaboration."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Nonverbal Communication"@en ;
