ngm:owl-class-hierarchy a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The OWL Class Hierarchy is the directed acyclic graph (DAG) of named and anonymous classes connected via rdfs:subClassOf axioms within a Web Ontology Language (OWL) ontology, imposing a partial order on the class extension lattice. It provides the primary vehicle for monotonic inheritance of properties and restrictions, enabling description-logic reasoners such as HermiT, Pellet, and FaCT++ to classify individuals, detect unsatisfiable classes, and compute implicit subsumption relationships that are not asserted explicitly. The hierarchy is closed under the OWL semantics of the chosen profile (OWL 2 DL, EL, QL, or RL), constraining the decidability and computational complexity of reasoning tasks performed over it. Well-engineered class hierarchies underpin interoperability across domains including biomedical ontologies (GO, SNOMED CT), geospatial standards, and knowledge-graph schemas."@en ;
    rdfs:label "OWL Class Hierarchy"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ontology-structure ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r15619 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r15620 ;
