ngm:payment-preimage a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A payment preimage is the secret value whose cryptographic hash forms a payment hash used to lock funds in a Hash Time-Locked Contract on the Lightning Network. Revealing the preimage proves that the intended recipient received the payment and simultaneously releases the locked funds along every hop of the payment route. It is the mechanism that lets protocols such as BOLT11 invoices and L402 guarantee atomic, trustless settlement across multi-hop payment channels."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Payment Preimage"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:lightning-network ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.55"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "payment-preimage" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "blockchain" .
ngm:payment-processing a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Payment processing is the sequence of operations that authorise, capture, clear and settle a monetary transaction between a payer and a payee. It coordinates merchants, payment gateways, networks and settlement institutions to verify funds, manage risk and move value reliably. Modern payment processing spans card rails, digital wallets and blockchain-based settlement, increasingly emphasising speed, fraud detection and interoperability."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Payment Processing"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:payment-network ;
