ngm:performance-monitoring a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Performance Monitoring is the continuous collection, analysis, and visualisation of metrics describing how a system, application, or model behaves under real workloads. It tracks indicators such as latency, throughput, error rates, resource utilisation, and, for machine-learning systems, predictive quality and drift, surfacing degradation through dashboards and alerts. Performance monitoring is a core observability discipline that enables teams to detect regressions, diagnose bottlenecks, and uphold service-level objectives."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Performance Monitoring"@en ;
