ngm:player-two-platform-implementation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Player Two code is the technical implementation layer of the Player Two platform, comprising a Vue.js front-end, BIP85-derived key management for trustless authentication, a Nostr-relay-based messaging architecture, and middleware whitelist logic. It enables encrypted group collaboration without server-held keys, using derivation path m/44'/1237 for per-user identity."@en ;
