    rdfs:label "Policy Circumvention"@en .
ngm:policy-decision-point a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Policy Decision Point (PDP) is the logical component in an attribute-based or policy-based access control architecture that evaluates access requests against a set of authorisation policies and returns a permit, deny, or indeterminate decision. The PDP receives a request context—including subject attributes, resource attributes, action, and environment conditions—from a Policy Enforcement Point (PEP), retrieves applicable policies from a Policy Information Point (PIP) or Policy Administration Point (PAP), and applies the XACML combining algorithms or equivalent logic to reach a binding decision. PDPs are the computational core of fine-grained, dynamic authorisation systems used in zero-trust security architectures, identity federation, API gateways, and cloud IAM platforms."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Policy Decision Point"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:access-control-system ;
