ngm:post-incident-review a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A post-incident review is a structured retrospective conducted after an operational incident to establish what happened, why, and how recurrence can be prevented. Conducted in a blameless manner, it reconstructs the timeline, identifies contributing factors through root-cause analysis, and produces tracked corrective actions and durable lessons. It is a core practice of incident management and site reliability engineering that turns failures into systemic improvement."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Post Incident Review"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:incident-management ;
