ngm:power-distribution-unit a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A power distribution unit (PDU) is a device that delivers and manages electrical power to multiple pieces of equipment within a data centre rack or row. It takes input from an upstream supply such as a UPS or the building electrical feed and distributes regulated, often metered, power across many outlets. Modern intelligent PDUs add remote monitoring, per-outlet switching and environmental sensing to support availability and energy-efficiency goals."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Power Distribution Unit"@en ;
