ngm:power-purchase-agreement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) is a long-term contract between an electricity generator and a buyer that fixes the price, volume and delivery terms for electrical energy over a defined period. PPAs underpin the financing of generation assets, particularly renewable plants, by guaranteeing a stable revenue stream that de-risks capital investment. They allocate market, volume and curtailment risk between producer and offtaker and may be physical or virtual (financial)."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Power Purchase Agreement"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:power-systems ;
