ngm:privacy-utility-tradeoffs a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Privacy-Utility Tradeoffs represent the fundamental tension in privacy-preserving AI between privacy preservation—protecting sensitive information through techniques such as differential privacy, anonymisation, or encryption—and model utility, which encompasses accuracy and other performance metrics necessary for effective decision-making. This tension is characterised by Pareto frontiers of achievable (privacy, utility) pairs where strengthening privacy typically degrades model performance and vice versa."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Privacy Utility Tradeoffs"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-governance-and-ethics ;
