ngm:procedural-memory a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The long-term memory subsystem that stores knowledge of how to perform actions and skills — as opposed to episodic memory of specific events or semantic memory of facts; in cognitive science it underlies habits and motor skills learnt through repetition, while in cognitive architectures and AI agents it is realised as production rules, learned policies, reusable workflows, or refined system prompts that encode competence rather than content."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Procedural Memory"@en ;
