ngm:process-reward-model a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A process reward model is a reward model that scores the individual intermediate steps of a model's reasoning trajectory rather than only its final answer. By supervising each step of a chain of thought, it provides dense, step-level feedback that guides search and reinforcement learning toward sound reasoning processes. Process reward models contrast with outcome reward models, which assign a single reward based solely on the final result."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Process Reward Model"@en ;
