ngm:rack-and-pinion-actuator a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A rack and pinion actuator is a mechanical transmission mechanism that converts rotary motion from a pinion gear into linear motion along a toothed rack, commonly used in robotics and industrial automation for precise linear positioning. The pinion rotates against the rack to produce controlled translational displacement, with speed and force determined by gear ratio and motor torque. It offers high stiffness, repeatability, and scalability for long-stroke linear axes in robotic manipulators and CNC systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Rack and Pinion Actuator"@en ;
