ngm:ragdoll-physics a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Ragdoll physics is a procedural animation technique that simulates the limp, physically reactive motion of an articulated character body using a system of rigid bodies connected by constrained joints. Instead of playing pre-authored animation, the character's limbs respond dynamically to gravity, collisions and impulses via a physics engine. It is widely used in games and interactive media to produce believable falls, impacts and death animations."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Ragdoll Physics"@en ;
