ngm:reasoning-engine a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A reasoning engine is a software component that derives new conclusions from a body of knowledge by applying logical inference rules, probabilistic methods, or learned heuristics. Classical reasoning engines operate over symbolic knowledge bases using forward or backward chaining, description-logic subsumption, or constraint solving, while modern neuro-symbolic and LLM-based engines combine learned language representations with structured tool use and search. Reasoning engines power expert systems, semantic-web query answering, automated planning, and multi-step problem solving in agentic AI systems. In the DreamLab mesh the reasoning engine is Whelk, an OWL 2 EL classifier that derives entailments and rejects contradictions before they enter the shared knowledge graph."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Engine"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:reasoning ;
    vc:enables ngm:chain-of-thought ;
    vc:enables ngm:multi-step-reasoning ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.8"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:llm-agents ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:semantic-web-linked-data-standard ;
    vc:slug "reasoning-engine" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "ai" ;
    vc:uses ngm:knowledge-graph .
ngm:reasoning-models a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Reasoning models are large language models trained or post-trained to generate extended intermediate chains of thought before producing a final answer, trading inference-time compute for higher accuracy on complex tasks. They are typically optimised with reinforcement learning on verifiable problems in mathematics, coding, and logic. By spending more tokens deliberating, they outperform standard models on multi-step problems where single-pass generation fails."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Models"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:large-language-models ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:frontier-models ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:prime-intellect ;
    vc:slug "reasoning-models" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "ai" .
ngm:reasoning-service a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Service"@en .
ngm:reasoning-token a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Token"@en .
ngm:reasoning-trace a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A reasoning trace is the recorded sequence of intermediate thoughts, tool calls, and decisions a model produces while solving a task, distinct from its final output. It serves as both a working scratchpad that improves accuracy and an audit artefact for inspecting how an agent reached a conclusion. Traces underpin debugging, evaluation, and self-correction in agentic systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoning Trace"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-agent-system ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:agents ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:computer-use-and-browser-agents ;
    vc:slug "reasoning-trace" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "ai" .
