    vc:sourceDomain "robotics" .
ngm:reference-implementation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A reference implementation is an authoritative, openly available realisation of a specification or standard that demonstrates how it is meant to be built and used. It serves as a concrete benchmark against which other implementations can be compared for correctness and conformance. By turning a written specification into working software, it reduces ambiguity and accelerates adoption of the standard."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Reference Implementation"@en ;
