ngm:replication-protocol a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A replication protocol is the set of rules and message exchanges by which a distributed system maintains multiple copies of data across nodes so that they remain consistent according to a chosen consistency model despite failures and concurrency. It governs how updates are propagated, ordered, and acknowledged, balancing availability, latency, and durability. Replication protocols range from synchronous primary-backup and quorum schemes to asynchronous gossip and conflict-free replicated approaches."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Replication Protocol"@en ;
