ngm:retail-cbdc a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A retail central bank digital currency (CBDC) is a digital form of sovereign money issued directly by a central bank for use by the general public in everyday payments. Unlike wholesale CBDCs, which serve interbank settlement, retail CBDCs target consumers and merchants and may use account-based or token-based designs over distributed or centralised ledgers. They aim to provide a public digital payment instrument with central-bank credit safety."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Retail CBDC"@en ;
