ngm:risk-weighted-assets a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Risk-weighted assets (RWA) are a bank's assets and off-balance-sheet exposures weighted according to their credit, market, and operational risk, forming the denominator of regulatory capital ratios. Under the Basel framework, riskier exposures attract higher weights, so banks must hold proportionally more capital against them. RWA links the composition of a bank's portfolio to its minimum capital requirements and overall solvency."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Risk Weighted Assets"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:capital-adequacy ;
