    rdfs:comment "A Robot Joint is a mechanical articulation between two robot links that permits controlled relative motion — rotational, translational, or compound — enabling the full kinematic range of a robotic arm or manipulator. Joint types include revolute, prismatic, and spherical, each characterised by degrees of freedom and load capacity."@en ;
