ngm:robotaxi a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A robotaxi is a self-driving vehicle operated as an on-demand ride-hailing service without a human safety driver, combining autonomous vehicle technology with fleet dispatch, mapping, and remote-assistance infrastructure. Passengers summon a robotaxi through a mobile application in the same manner as a conventional ride-hailing service, but the vehicle navigates, avoids obstacles, and completes the trip using onboard perception and planning systems. Commercial robotaxi deployments require regulatory approval and typically operate within geofenced service areas where the vehicle's autonomy stack has been extensively validated."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Robotaxi"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:autonomous-vehicle ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18449 ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:requires ngm:autonomous-vehicle ;
    vc:slug "robotaxi" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "robotics" .
ngm:robotic-arm a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A robotic arm is a programmable mechanical manipulator, typically composed of rigid links connected by actuated joints, that positions and orients an end-effector within a workspace. Its degrees of freedom allow it to reach and manipulate objects under the control of motion-planning and kinematics algorithms. Robotic arms range from industrial units performing repetitive high-precision tasks to collaborative arms designed to work safely alongside people. They are a foundational platform across manufacturing, surgery, logistics and research."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Robotic Arm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:manipulator ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18450 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18451 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18452 ;
