ngm:runbook a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A runbook is a documented set of procedures for operating, maintaining and recovering a system, giving operators a repeatable sequence of steps for routine tasks and known failure scenarios. Modern runbooks range from human-readable checklists to executable automations that orchestrate remediation directly. They are a core artefact of site reliability engineering, reducing reliance on individual expertise during incidents."@en ;
