ngm:safety-assessment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Safety assessment is a systematic analytical process that identifies, evaluates, and mitigates hazards associated with a system, product, or operational process to demonstrate that residual risk is tolerable within accepted standards and regulatory frameworks. It encompasses methods such as Failure Modes and Effects Analysis (FMEA), Fault Tree Analysis (FTA), Hazard and Operability Studies (HAZOP), and probabilistic safety analysis, applied across domains including aerospace, automotive, nuclear, medical devices, and increasingly AI systems. Safety assessments form the evidentiary basis for certification against safety standards such as IEC 61508 and ISO 26262."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Safety Assessment"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:risk-assessment ;
    vc:enables ngm:ai-risk-assessment ;
    vc:enables ngm:safety-critical-systems ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-draft ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.8"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:iec-61508 ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:iso-26262 ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:safety-standard ;
    vc:slug "safety-assessment" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "governance" ;
    vc:uses ngm:functional-safety ;
    vc:uses ngm:hazard-analysis ;
    vc:uses ngm:risk-assessment-methodology .
ngm:safety-assurance a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Safety assurance is the systematic process of building and demonstrating justified confidence that a system will operate safely throughout its lifecycle. It draws on hazard analysis, structured safety cases, verification evidence, and continuous monitoring to argue that residual risk is acceptable. For autonomous and industrial systems it provides the evidentiary basis for deployment and regulatory acceptance."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Safety Assurance"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:robo-safety-and-standards ;
    skos:broader ngm:robo-safety-and-standards ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-emerging ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:predictive-maintenance ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:robo-navigation-and-planning ;
    vc:slug "safety-assurance" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "robotics" .
ngm:safety-case a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A safety case is a structured, evidence-backed argument that a system is acceptably safe to operate in a defined context and operational environment. It comprises explicit safety claims, the reasoning that connects them, and the supporting evidence drawn from hazard analysis, design measures, verification, and operational data. Commonly documented using notations such as the Goal Structuring Notation or Claims-Arguments-Evidence, the safety case is reviewed by stakeholders and regulators and maintained throughout the system lifecycle. It is the central assurance artefact in safety-critical and autonomous-systems engineering."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Safety Case"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:functional-safety ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18672 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18673 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18674 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18675 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r18676 ;
