ngm:satellite-communication a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Satellite communication is the use of artificial Earth-orbiting satellites as relay stations to transmit signals — including voice, data, video, and telemetry — between ground terminals separated by large distances or challenging terrain. Signals are uplinked from a ground station to a satellite transponder, which amplifies and retransmits them on a different frequency to one or more receiving terminals. Different orbital regimes (GEO, MEO, LEO) offer distinct trade-offs between coverage footprint, latency, and capacity."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Satellite Communication"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:infrastructure ;
