ngm:satellite-monitoring a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Satellite monitoring is the use of orbital remote-sensing platforms to observe and measure conditions on the Earth's surface over time. In sustainability and supply-chain contexts it supports verification of deforestation, land use, emissions plumes, and facility activity using multispectral, radar, and thermal imagery. The resulting geospatial data feeds carbon accounting, compliance, and ethical-sourcing assessments."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Satellite Monitoring"@en ;
