ngm:self-service-portal a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A self-service portal is a customer-facing software interface that lets users resolve requests -- account changes, order tracking, troubleshooting -- without contacting a human agent, often backed by AI-driven search, chatbots or workflow automation. It reduces support-team load by handling routine, well-defined requests automatically while escalating complex cases to human agents. Self-service portals are a common deliverable of customer service and customer support automation initiatives."@en ;
