ngm:semi-fungible-token a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A blockchain token standard that combines fungible and non-fungible properties, typically implemented under ERC-1155. Semi-fungible tokens represent classes of interchangeable assets (e.g. event tickets of the same tier) that may transition to uniquely non-fungible assets upon redemption or use, enabling a single contract to manage both fungible currencies and unique collectibles with reduced gas costs."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Semi-Fungible Token"@en ;
