ngm:simulated-annealing a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A stochastic metaheuristic for global optimisation, inspired by the annealing of metals, that explores a solution space via local moves while accepting worsening solutions with a probability governed by a gradually decreasing temperature parameter, allowing early escape from local optima and increasingly greedy refinement as the temperature cools; widely applied to combinatorial problems such as travelling salesman routing, chip placement, scheduling and logistics."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Simulated Annealing"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:heuristic-methods ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-draft ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.8"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:combinatorial-optimisation ;
    vc:slug "simulated-annealing" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "artificial-intelligence" ;
    vc:uses ngm:local-search .
ngm:simulation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Simulation is the computational reproduction of real-world systems, physical phenomena, or abstract processes through mathematical models that evolve over time, enabling experimentation, training, and prediction without risk to personnel or infrastructure. Simulations span a fidelity spectrum from simplified discrete-event models to high-fidelity continuous-physics environments powered by physics engines, rendering pipelines, and stochastic solvers. In spatial computing and metaverse contexts, real-time simulation underpins immersive training, digital twin synchronisation, and AI agent incubation. Simulation outputs are validated against empirical data and uncertainty quantified to ensure transferability of findings to the real world."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Simulation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:digital-twin ;
