ngm:smart-contract-deployment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Smart contract deployment is the process of compiling contract source code to bytecode and publishing it to a blockchain, after which the contract acquires a fixed on-chain address and becomes callable by other accounts and contracts. It typically involves development frameworks that handle compilation, testing, gas estimation, and network submission. Deployment is irreversible on most chains, so verification and testing precede it as standard practice."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Deployment"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:smart-contract ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-draft ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.55"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "smart-contract-deployment" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "blockchain" .
ngm:smart-contract-deployment-pipeline a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Deployment Pipeline"@en .
ngm:smart-contract-development a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Development"@en .
ngm:smart-contract-development-framework a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Development Framework"@en .
ngm:smart-contract-enforcement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Smart contract enforcement is the property by which the terms encoded in a self-executing on-chain program are carried out automatically and irreversibly once predefined conditions are met, without requiring trust in a counterparty or intermediary. Enforcement derives from the deterministic execution of code on a distributed ledger and the immutability of recorded state. It reduces reliance on external legal recourse while raising questions of how code-based outcomes interact with conventional contract law."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Enforcement"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:smart-contract ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:arbitration-process ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:non-repudiation ;
    vc:slug "smart-contract-enforcement" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "blockchain" .
ngm:smart-contract-event-decoding a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Event Decoding"@en .
ngm:smart-contract-execution a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Smart contract execution is the deterministic, on-chain processing of immutable bytecode deployed at a specific blockchain address, triggered by an inbound transaction and evaluated identically by every validating node in the network. Execution occurs within a sandboxed virtual machine—such as the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) or Solana Virtual Machine (SVM)—which enforces gas or fee metering to bound computation costs, maintains state isolation, and guarantees identical outputs across all nodes given the same inputs and world state. The execution model encompasses transaction ingestion, opcode interpretation, state transition application, event emission, and atomicity enforcement, with failed executions reverting all state changes. Smart contract execution underpins trustless multi-party agreements, decentralised finance protocols, non-fungible token operations, cross-chain messaging, and decentralised autonomous organisations without reliance on a central intermediary."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Contract Execution"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:bc-protocol-and-consensus ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19458 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19459 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19460 ;
