ngm:smart-home a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A smart home is a residence equipped with networked devices, sensors, and actuators that can be monitored and controlled remotely or automated to respond to conditions and occupant preferences. Smart homes integrate lighting, climate control, security, appliances, and entertainment through a common connectivity fabric and often a central hub or voice assistant. They build on Internet of Things technologies, wireless mesh networking, and interoperability standards to deliver convenience, energy efficiency, and accessibility."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Home"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:internet-of-things ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19496 ;
