ngm:spaced-repetition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Spaced repetition is a learning technique that schedules reviews of material at increasing intervals timed to occur just before predicted forgetting, exploiting the psychological spacing effect to strengthen long-term retention efficiently. Algorithmic implementations track each item's review history and recall outcomes to compute the optimal next-review date, concentrating study effort on material at risk of being forgotten. It is a core mechanism in flashcard software and the memory-management components of adaptive learning systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Spaced Repetition"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:adaptive-learning ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19735 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r19736 ;
