ngm:spectral-clustering a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A clustering technique that partitions data using the eigenvectors of a graph Laplacian built from a pairwise similarity matrix. By embedding points into the subspace spanned by the Laplacian's smallest eigenvectors and running a simple algorithm such as k-means in that spectral space, it relaxes NP-hard graph-cut objectives (ratio cut, normalised cut) into tractable eigenproblems, allowing it to recover non-convex, connectivity-defined clusters that centroid-based methods cannot separate."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Spectral Clustering"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:clustering ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
