    rdfs:comment "STRIPS (Stanford Research Institute Problem Solver) is a classical automated planning formalism that represents world states as conjunctions of propositions and defines actions via precondition, add-list, and delete-list operators. It introduced the core abstraction underlying modern planning languages such as PDDL and remains foundational to symbolic AI planning."@en ;
