ngm:structural-member a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Structural Member is a discrete load-bearing component of a robotic system's physical frame, such as a link, beam, bracket, or chassis element, that transmits forces and torques between joints or actuators. Structural members define the kinematic chain of a robot and their geometric and material properties directly constrain workspace, payload, and dynamic performance."@en ;
