ngm:surface-normal a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A surface normal is a vector perpendicular to a surface at a given point, indicating the orientation of that surface in space. Normals are fundamental to lighting and shading calculations, because the angle between a normal and a light direction governs how much illumination a surface receives. In computer graphics and 3D reconstruction, surface normals drive realistic shading, normal mapping, and the recovery of fine geometric detail."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Surface Normal"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:scene-geometry ;
