ngm:task-analysis a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Task analysis is the systematic study of how users accomplish goals, decomposing activities into the sequence of actions, decisions, and cognitive operations required to complete them. It produces structured descriptions such as hierarchical task models and workflow maps that inform interface design, error prevention, and training. By making implicit work practices explicit, it grounds design decisions in observed user behaviour rather than assumption."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Task Analysis"@en ;
