ngm:telemetry a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Telemetry is the automated collection, transmission and aggregation of measurements and signals from remote or distributed systems to a central point for monitoring and analysis. In software and infrastructure it commonly refers to the emission of metrics, logs, traces and events that describe a system's behaviour and health. Telemetry data is the raw substrate on which observability, alerting and performance analysis are built."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Telemetry"@en ;
