ngm:temporal-entity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A temporal entity is an ontological category for anything that exists in or is defined by time, such as an instant, an interval, an event, or a process. In knowledge representation it serves as a shared superclass that anchors time-bearing concepts so they can be related by ordering, duration, and containment. The notion follows established time ontologies like the W3C OWL-Time vocabulary."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Temporal Entity"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:entity ;
