ngm:tensor a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A tensor is a multidimensional array of numerical values characterised by a rank, a shape and a data type, generalising scalars, vectors and matrices to arbitrary dimensions. In machine learning it is the fundamental data structure that holds inputs, parameters, activations and gradients as they flow through a model. Tensor operations such as contraction, broadcasting and elementwise functions are the computational primitives executed on accelerators during training and inference."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Tensor"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:linear-algebra ;
