ngm:texture-map a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Texture Map is a 2D image applied to the surface of a 3D model to add visual detail such as colour, roughness, normals, or emissive properties without increasing polygon count. Texture maps are indexed via UV coordinates that establish a correspondence between surface points and image pixels. They are a foundational component of real-time and offline rendering pipelines."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Texture Map"@en ;
