ngm:thermodynamics a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Thermodynamics is the branch of physics concerned with heat, work, temperature and energy, and the laws governing their transformation and the direction of spontaneous processes. Its core principles - conservation of energy, the increase of entropy, and absolute-zero limits - underpin engineering of engines, cooling and energy systems. In computing infrastructure it constrains power consumption, heat dissipation and the efficiency of data-centre cooling."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Thermodynamics"@en ;
