ngm:third-party-assurance a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Third-party assurance is the independent verification of an organisation's claims, disclosures, or controls by a party with no stake in the outcome, producing an assurance opinion that stakeholders can rely on more readily than self-reported data. It is commonly required for emissions reporting, carbon neutrality claims, and financial statements, where an accredited external auditor examines evidence against a recognised standard. It differs from internal audit in that independence from the reporting entity is the source of its credibility."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Third-Party Assurance"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:audit ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:isPartOf ngm:audit ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.6"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "third-party-assurance" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "governance" .
ngm:third-party-auditing a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Third-party auditing is the independent examination of an organisation's systems, processes, controls, or claims by an external party that has no stake in the outcome, in order to provide credible assurance to stakeholders. By separating the auditor from the audited, it strengthens trust, accountability, and regulatory compliance beyond what self-assessment can offer. In technology and AI governance it covers security audits, conformity assessment, and verification of model or supply-chain claims."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Third Party Auditing"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:audit ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r20799 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r20800 ;
