ngm:threat-modelling a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Threat modelling is a structured security engineering process that identifies, enumerates, and prioritises potential threats to a system by reasoning systematically about adversaries, attack vectors, and mitigations before or during design. It produces an explicit model of what can go wrong, enabling security controls to be allocated proportionally to risk, and is applied across software, hardware, and AI systems throughout the development lifecycle."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Threat Modelling"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:risk-assessment ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r20826 ;
