ngm:throughput a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Throughput is the rate at which a system completes useful work over a unit of time, such as requests served per second, tokens generated per second or bytes transferred per second. It measures sustained productive capacity rather than the time to complete a single operation. In machine learning serving it captures how many inferences or training samples a system can process under load. Maximising throughput typically involves batching, parallelism and resource utilisation, often trading off against per-request latency."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Throughput"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:ai-infrastructure ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:performance-metrics ;
