ngm:throughput-optimisation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The systems discipline of maximising useful work completed per unit time — requests, tokens, or samples per second — on fixed hardware, typically by batching to raise arithmetic intensity, keeping accelerators saturated through scheduling and overlap, and managing memory so that capacity rather than stalls bounds concurrency, usually traded off explicitly against per-request latency."@en ;
