    rdfs:comment "A timer is a software or hardware mechanism that measures elapsed time or schedules an action to occur after a delay or at a recurring interval. In collaborative and real-time applications it provides shared countdowns, time-boxing, and synchronised triggers that all participants observe consistently. Timers are a basic building block of event scheduling, animation, and time-bounded interaction."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Timer"@en ;
