ngm:underwater-robot a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "An Underwater Robot is a robotic platform designed to operate in aquatic environments, encompassing Remotely Operated Vehicles (ROVs) tethered for real-time control and Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs) executing pre-programmed or AI-guided missions. Applications include deep-sea scientific survey, offshore infrastructure inspection, marine conservation, and defence, with platforms rated from hundreds to thousands of metres depth."@en ;
