ngm:uv-mapping a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "UV mapping is the process of projecting a 3D model's surface onto a two-dimensional coordinate space so that texture images can be applied accurately to its geometry. The letters U and V denote the axes of this 2D texture space, distinct from the X, Y, and Z axes of the model. By unwrapping the mesh into UV islands, artists control how textures, normal maps, and other surface data wrap around the object with minimal stretching or seams."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Uv Mapping"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:3d-modelling ;
