ngm:voronoi-diagram a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Voronoi diagram is a partition of a plane (or higher-dimensional space) into regions based on proximity to a set of seed points, where each region contains all locations closer to its seed than to any other. It is a foundational structure in computational geometry, dual to the Delaunay triangulation, and supports nearest-neighbour queries, spatial interpolation and procedural generation. Voronoi tessellations appear across spatial analysis, graphics and natural sciences."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Voronoi Diagram"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:computational-geometry ;
