ngm:vulnerability-analysis a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Vulnerability analysis is the systematic process of discovering, characterising, and prioritising weaknesses in software, systems, or networks that could be exploited to compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability. It combines static and dynamic code inspection, configuration review, and exploitability assessment to feed remediation and risk decisions. Unlike threat modelling, which is attacker-centric and design-stage, vulnerability analysis focuses on concrete flaws in deployed or candidate artefacts."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Vulnerability Analysis"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:cybersecurity ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:risk-assessment ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:threat-modelling ;
    vc:slug "vulnerability-analysis" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "security" .
ngm:vulnerability-assessment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Vulnerability assessment is the structured evaluation of an organisation's systems against known weaknesses, producing a prioritised inventory of exposures and recommended mitigations. It is typically scope-bounded and recurring, using automated scanners and authenticated checks to map findings to severity and asset criticality. Mandated by many cybersecurity standards, it provides the baseline evidence for compliance and continuous risk reduction."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Vulnerability Assessment"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:cybersecurity ;
    vc:hasMaturity ngmi:maturity-established ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.72"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:cybersecurity-standard ;
    vc:relatedTo ngm:threat-modelling ;
    vc:slug "vulnerability-assessment" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "security" .
