ngm:web-access-control a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Web Access Control (WAC) is a decentralised authorisation system for web resources that uses RDF-based access control lists to specify which agents may read, write, append, or control linked-data resources identified by URIs. It is a core mechanism in the Solid ecosystem, letting individuals govern access to their personal data pods using WebID-based identity. WAC decouples authorisation from any central server, aligning with self-sovereign data principles."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Web Access Control"@en ;
