ngm:wheel-odometry a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Wheel odometry is a method of estimating a mobile robot's change in position and orientation by counting wheel rotations measured with encoders and applying a kinematic motion model. As an instance of dead reckoning, it integrates incremental wheel displacement over time to track pose relative to a starting point. It is simple and low-cost but accumulates drift from wheel slip, uneven terrain and calibration error, so it is typically fused with other sensors."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Wheel Odometry"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:odometry ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r22484 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r22485 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r22486 ;
