ngm:x509-standard a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The X.509 standard defines the format of public-key certificates that bind a public key to an identity, together with the structures for certificate paths and revocation lists used in public-key infrastructure. An X.509 certificate carries fields such as subject, issuer, validity period, public key and extensions, and is signed by a certificate authority so that relying parties can verify it by tracing a chain to a trusted root. It is the foundational certificate format underlying TLS, secure email and many authentication systems."@en ;
    rdfs:label "X509 Standard"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:digital-certificate ;
