ngm:zero-day-exploits a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A zero-day exploit is an attack technique that targets a software or hardware vulnerability unknown to the vendor and for which no patch yet exists, giving defenders zero days to prepare. Because the flaw is undisclosed, such exploits bypass signature-based defenses and are highly valuable to attackers, state actors, and exploit brokers. They matter as a central concern in cybersecurity, surveillance, and offensive cyber operations."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Zero-Day Exploits"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:cybersecurity ;
